Usage: agent-deck fleet status [options]

Report sessions the registry believes are alive whose tmux session is
gone. Read-only: no restarts, no writes.

With --group-by-credential the report additionally groups every
auth-401-held session by WHICH credential is dead, so one dead token
reads as one line instead of N per-session failures. Opt-in: without
the flag the output is exactly the per-session view it has always been.
The grouping is computed locally and never leaves the machine.

Options:
  -confirm-delay duration
    	Delay between confirming probes (default 750ms)
  -confirm-probes int
    	Independent tmux probes that must agree a session is gone before it counts as down (default 2)
  -dead-fraction float
    	Share of should-be-alive sessions that must be down for a mass-death verdict (default 0.5)
  -group string
    	Only consider sessions in this group path (and its descendants)
  -group-by-credential
    	Group auth-401-held sessions by which credential is dead and report one escalation per credential (opt-in, local-only; off by default the per-session view is unchanged)
  -include-idle
    	Also treat status=idle sessions as down (off by default: idle is also the status of a session that was never started)
  -json
    	Output as JSON
  -min-dead int
    	Minimum down sessions for the shape to be reported as a mass death (default 3)
  -q	Minimal output (short)
  -quiet
    	Minimal output
